**DEFINITION 8.3.** A retraction $a : E \to E$ is called a *projection* provided

$$a \sqsubseteq 1_E;$$

it is *finitary* iff its fixed-point set is isomorphic to a domain. $\square$

The development is with the [projection](1980_projection.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`definition_83`).** An endomap is a projection precisely when it is a retraction below the identity, and a finitary projection precisely when it is both a projection and finitary (fixed points isomorphic to a domain).

*Proof.* By the definitions of projection and finitary projection. ∎
